  "description": "FAGZEW crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C94 H98 N20 Nd6 O48,C2 H6 O1,3(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 10 O neighbors; Nd3 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd4 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd5 (Nd) has 10 O neighbors; Nd6 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 4 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a chain with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.659-3.721 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 92.97-100.95°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C100H118.24N20Nd6O51.96.",
